{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QuantumUniverses.CategoricalHodgeStar","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QuantumUniverses.CategoricalHodgeStar","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.Basic","lean:module:QOU.Glossary","lean:module:Mathlib.CategoryTheory.Monoidal.Category","lean:module:Mathlib.CategoryTheory.Functor.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.CategoryTheory.NatTrans","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Group.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Ring.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Order.Field.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Real.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Analysis.SpecialFunctions.Pow.Real","lean:module:Mathlib.Topology.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Topology.ContinuousMap.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Geometry.Manifold.IsManifold.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Analysis.InnerProductSpace.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.LinearAlgebra.ExteriorAlgebra.Basic"],"declarations":11,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.HodgeInvolution.IsAntiSelfDual","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.HodgeInvolution.IsAntiSelfDual","kind":"def","line":64,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-universes/categorical-hodge-star.lean#L64-L67","doc":"An element `v : V` is **anti-self-dual** if `⋆(v) = -v`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.HodgeInvolution.IsSelfDual","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.HodgeInvolution.IsSelfDual","kind":"def","line":59,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-universes/categorical-hodge-star.lean#L59-L62","doc":"An element `v : V` is **self-dual** if `⋆(v) = v`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.HodgeInvolution.star_sq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.HodgeInvolution.star_sq","kind":"theorem","line":57,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-universes/categorical-hodge-star.lean#L57-L57","doc":"Involutivity: `⋆(⋆(v)) = v` for all `v`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.HodgeInvolution.star","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.HodgeInvolution.star","kind":"def","line":55,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-universes/categorical-hodge-star.lean#L55-L55","doc":"The Hodge star `⋆ : V → V`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.HodgeInvolution.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.HodgeInvolution.mk","kind":"ctor","line":53,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-universes/categorical-hodge-star.lean#L53-L53","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.HodgeInvolution","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.HodgeInvolution","kind":"structure","line":51,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-universes/categorical-hodge-star.lean#L51-L57","doc":"An **involution on a type** (concrete version for the ℂ realisation).\nModels the Hodge star acting pointwise on sections of a bundle. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.CatHodgeInvolution.IsSelfDual","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.CatHodgeInvolution.IsSelfDual","kind":"def","line":45,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-universes/categorical-hodge-star.lean#L45-L49","doc":"A morphism `f : Y ⟶ X` is **self-dual** w.r.t. a categorical Hodge\ninvolution if `f ≫ ⋆ = f`, i.e. `f` lands in the `+1`-eigenspace. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.CatHodgeInvolution.star_sq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.CatHodgeInvolution.star_sq","kind":"theorem","line":43,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-universes/categorical-hodge-star.lean#L43-L43","doc":"Involutivity: `⋆ ≫ ⋆ = id_X`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.CatHodgeInvolution.star","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.CatHodgeInvolution.star","kind":"def","line":41,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-universes/categorical-hodge-star.lean#L41-L41","doc":"The Hodge star operator `⋆ : X ⟶ X`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.CatHodgeInvolution.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.CatHodgeInvolution.mk","kind":"ctor","line":38,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-universes/categorical-hodge-star.lean#L38-L38","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.CatHodgeInvolution","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.CatHodgeInvolution","kind":"structure","line":33,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-universes/categorical-hodge-star.lean#L33-L43","doc":"An **involutive endomorphism** in a category, modeling the Hodge star\noperator `⋆`.  When `⋆² = id`, the eigenvalue decomposition\n`V = V⁺ ⊕ V⁻` (self-dual ⊕ anti-self-dual) follows from the spectral\ntheory of involutions.  This is the most general setting: works over any\nfield, in any category with an identity. ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:def:categorical-hodge-star","label":"def:categorical-hodge-star","md":"quantum-observable-universe/quantum-universes/categorical-hodge-star.md"}],"signatureChunk":0}]}